## Format Change

**v2 (current):**
```
[16-byte MD5][2-byte length][N-byte EDID]
```

**v3 (proposed):**
```
[6-byte ID][2-byte length][N-byte EDID]
```

Savings: 10 bytes per entry × 142k = ~1.4 MB

## GitHub Path Computation

Full path can be computed from EDID bytes + vendor mapping:

```javascript
function edidToGitHubUrl(edidBytes, id, vendorMapping) {
  // Type: byte 20, bit 7
  const type = (edidBytes[20] & 0x80) ? "Digital" : "Analog";

  // Vendor code: bytes 8-9 (EISA 3-char)
  const code = decodeVendorCode(edidBytes.slice(8, 10));

  // Model: vendor code + product (bytes 10-11, little-endian)
  const product = (edidBytes[11] << 8) | edidBytes[10];
  const model = `${code}${product.toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(4, '0')}`;

  // Vendor name from mapping
  const vendor = vendorMapping[code] || code;

  return `https://github.com/linuxhw/EDID/blob/master/${type}/${vendor}/${model}/${id}`;
}
```

## Data Files

1. **buckets/*.bin** - Updated format with 6-byte IDs
2. **vendors.json** - 1137 vendor code→name mappings (~21 KB)

## Validation Results

- Digital/Analog: 100% computable from EDID
- Model directory: 99.99% computable
- ID: 99.90% computable (matches linuxhw filenames)
- Vendor name: Requires ~21KB mapping table
